{"text": "Nichole Stefanow\n\nWork History\nSept 2013\u2014Present, Family & Youth Initiatives\nWomen\u2019s Network Director: train staff and volunteers; ensure needs are met for 3 networks\nEstablish reporting criteria, track data and prepare monthly/quarterly reports for grantors;\nMaintain PRC records for county Job & Family Services\nCoordinate and facilitate classes for clients; coordinate fundraisers with sponsors\n\nJuly 2009\u2014July 2015, Premier Designs Jewelry\nDirect Sales Consultant: schedule dates and demonstrate in homes\nEducate women using accessories to build confidence and self esteem\nHelp plan and facilitate monthly training for local unit\nMaintained downline of 4-7 representatives, helping them achieve their goals\n\nJuly 1999-\u2014 Dec 2005, Pampered Chef\nDirect Sales Consultant: scheduled dates and kitchen demonstrations in homes\nEducated guests on proper use of kitchen tools\n\nSept 1994\u2014 June 2007, Home Educator\nResponsible for education of 4 children grades K-12\nPrepared lesson plans and curriculum, kept grades\nReported records to Ohio Education Dept.\n\nVolunteer History\n2008\u2014Present, Fairborn Women\u2019s Network\nMentoring clients in pregnancy and parenting, using lessons provided\nAssistant Coordinator in 2010, helping with administrative duties\nCoordinator in 2012, coordinate and facilitate additional classes and educational opportunities for clients\n\n1993-2011, Maple Ave. Church of God\nHeld several board and committee positions throughout 19 years\nTaught children, youth and adults\nYouth Counselor and Fundraiser Coordinator\u2014 years\nNewcomer and Fellowship Coordinator\u201410 yearrs\n\nEducation\n1983, High School Diploma, North High School, Eastlake , Ohio\nComputer Programming Certificate\u2014Willoughby/Eastlake Technical Center\n\nReferences\nAvailable upon request",
